# Atlas.ti Backup Sync — Push Before AI Work

The live Atlas.ti project database lives **outside** this workspace:

```
C:\Users\dtlut\AppData\Roaming\Scientific Software\ATLASti.25\Libraries25\
```

This folder has its own git repo with remote `origin` → `https://github.com/Luttik/atlas-thesis-backup` (private).

## Rule

**Before augmenting any Atlas.ti data with AI** (editing codes, memos, quotations, or running import/export scripts), always ensure the latest Atlas.ti files are pushed to the backup repo.

Run this first:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\dtlut\AppData\Roaming\Scientific Software\ATLASti.25\Libraries25"
git add .
git commit -m "Sync before AI augmentation $(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm')"
git push
```

If there is nothing to commit, confirm with `git status` that the working tree is clean before proceeding.

> **Why**: Atlas.ti has no undo for external changes. A pushed backup before any AI-driven edits ensures you can always recover the exact pre-edit state.
